the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuplet element is present when a tuplet is to b